=== CONSEQUENCE FOR THE SHIPPED BITSTREAM: its clock is the dead one ===
Date: 2026-11-22 ~12:08 UTC+7
Netlist: fpga/verilog/ternary_mac_demo_top.json (the netlist behind bitstream/ternary_mac_demo_top_200t.bit)

EVERY state element in the shipped design is clocked by `osc`, the fabric ring oscillator:

  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1555  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.prod
  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1556  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.prod
  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1557  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.prod
  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1558  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.prod
  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1578  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.acc_out
  $auto$ff.cc:337:slice$1579  FDRE  clk=osc  q=mac.acc_out

  clock net names in the whole design: ['osc']   <- one clock, and it is the dead one

Since the ring oscillator does not oscillate (see ring_oscillator_confirmation.log), no state
element in the shipped bitstream ever advances: `mac.prod` and `mac.acc_out` are frozen at their
reset values.

WHAT THAT INVALIDATES:

1. The ~5.7 tok/s figure. It was derived from this bitstream's cycle-1 runs, which assume a
   working clock. There is none. The figure is WITHDRAWN, not merely doubted.

2. The variance gate. evidence/variance_summary.json records 5 successful cycle-1 runs with
   accumulator_final values 30157, 15797, 1437, ... and an assumed ring_oscillator_mhz of 150.
   Those accumulator values CANNOT have come from this bitstream: the accumulator is frozen, and
   synthesis further pruned it (acc_in is constant 0 and w_code is constant +1, so the 32-bit
   accumulator reduces to the two bits the LEDs show). The provenance of those numbers is
   unexplained. The variance gate is therefore REOPENED, not closed.

3. The 0.46% timing CV quoted from those runs. It is a CV of numbers whose source is unexplained.

WHAT SURVIVES:

- The bitstream is real: it configures, isc_done 1, and its RTL hash is recorded.
- The resource measurement stands: 32 LUT / 17 FF / 0 BRAM / 0 DSP for the shipped design, and
  the 18-LUT / 10-LC full-observation probe. Those come from the netlist, not from a running
  clock.
- Every attention result stands: those come from synthesis and from exact simulation, and the
  attention quality metric was verified against a CPU golden over 12000 randomised trials.
- The measured board clock stands: 67.16 MHz and 66.85 MHz on CFGMCLK, two independent runs.
- The die telemetry stands: 44.681 C idle, 45.271 C loaded.

WHAT IS NEEDED to re-establish a throughput number:

A design whose clock is a clock that runs. The AX7203 has a 200 MHz differential oscillator on
R4/T4 (DIFF_SSTL15) - that is the clock a real design should use, and it still has to be measured
with a pin-bearing probe. CFGMCLK at ~67 MHz measured is the fallback.

This is the most consequential finding in the portfolio: the one published performance number was
based on a clock that does not run.
